    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2610",
      "problem": "Solve for $x$ in the figure below given that $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{CD}$ is the perpendicular bisector of $\\overline{AB}.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14173511/assets/2dea948c7ab1cf3bb7f543c651d98f23cda8531bbec8cc44e12736c3f04f04c3.png)",
      "worked_solution": "By the perpendicular bisector theorem, a point on the perpendicular bisector of a segment is equidistant from the endpoints of the segment. Hence, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DA & =DB \\\\ x+5 & =2x \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
